 "pages": "p.3 (electrical: VD, data format), p.4 (pins), p.5-6 (timing, Table 1), p.13-17 (modes, CONVST, BUSY/INT, power-down, reading results), p.17-18 (TAG, averaging, FIFO, interrupts, reset), p.19-20 (Figures 28-30, Table 7), p.21-24 (CCR/SCR maps)",
 "notModeled": [
  "analog inputs, PGA gains, single-ended/differential pairing (stored only); the result is always the 0 V code 000h",
  "conversion time: CONVST to data = 8.5 tOSC acquisition + 13.5 tOSC conversion = 22 x 250 ns = 5500 ns (internal 4 MHz oscillator, up to 20 % variance not modeled); BUSY really goes low up to 8.5 tOSC after CONVST",
  "ADC trigger modes: idle (000b), manual trigger with delay mux (Mode 3), auto trigger with manual channel (Mode 4) and auto single-scan (Mode 5) are stored only; Mode 6 (auto multi-scan) is modeled as continuous on the selected channel without auto channel increment, first conversion by CONVST",
  "SPI-issued convert start (ADC SCR D0 = 1: each ADC read starts the next conversion)",
  "8-word FIFO, FIFO interrupts, scan-data-ready interrupt, FIFO level/status bits; the Interrupt SCR read-back of generated interrupts (the model reads back the enables)",
  "averaging modes (fast/accurate, 4/8/16 results; averaging bits D3:D2 of the read frame stay 0) and the programmable conversion delay",
  "TAG SE/Diff bit polarity is not given; it is output as 0",
  "SDO outputs all 1s in the frame right after a reset",
  "power-down (Interrupt SCR D7) and the rule that most registers may only be written in ADC idle mode",
  "register read: SDO shows the ADC result bits (not X X X 00000) in the first 8 bits of the frame",
  "SPI mode is not stated; mode 0 from Figure 3 (first bit at CS fall)"
 ],
